# Words vim's dictionary does not know but this work uses constantly.
#
# Shape-based false positives (ticket refs, ALLCAPS, snake_case, anything with a
# digit, code spans, URLs, paths) are handled in after/syntax/markdown.vim, not
# here — adding them one at a time would never converge. This file is for real
# words: domain vocabulary, tool names, and the technical terms that are simply
# missing from en_US.
#
# Add one interactively with `zg` (good) or `zw` (wrong); vim appends here and
# recompiles the .spl automatically. Keep this file sorted-ish by section.
#
# NOTE: vim treats a leading '#' as a comment only in the sense that it is an
# unlikely word; lines here are still loaded. That is harmless.

